t sequence of O_C-modules 0 -> W_4 -> W -> W_5 -> 0 with W_4, W_5 invertible of fibrewise degrees d_4, d_5 satisfying (D1) d_4 - n > 2g - 2 and (D2) d_5 - n = 2g - 2. Let phi : pi_*W -> pi_*(W|_Gamma) be evaluation, Z_ev := V(Fit_0(coker phi)) the Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure locus with its determinantal/Fitting scheme structure, N := omega_{C/B} tensor W_5^vee(Gamma) (invertible of fibrewise degree 0 by (D2)), a_N : B -> Pic^0_{C/B} its classifying morphism and e the identity section. Then: (T1) pi_*W and pi_*(W|_Gamma) are locally free of ranks d_4 + d_5 + 2 - 2g and 2n, so Fit_0(coker phi) = I_{2n}(phi); (T2) on P := Pic^0_{C/B}, with L_univ := omega_{C_P/P}(Gamma_P) tensor Poin^{-1} and Phi : p_*L_univ -> p_*(L_univ|_{Gamma_P}) the universal evaluation, one has the exact equality of ideal sheaves J := Fit_0(coker Phi) = I_e, both inclusions, over every such B; (T3) Fit_0(coker phi) = Fit_0(coker phi_5) with phi_5 : pi_*W_5 -> pi_*(W_5|_Gamma), using only the filtration and never a splitting W = W_4 direct-sum W_5; (T4) Fit_0(coker phi) = a_N^{-1}(I_e).O_B, i.e. Z_ev = a_N^{-1}(e(B)) as closed subschemes of B; (T5) formation of both sides commutes with arbitrary base change, and for every locally Noetherian B-scheme T the map T -> B factors through Z_ev if and only if N|_{C_T} is relatively trivial (isomorphic to pi_T^*M for some invertible M on T), whence the identification descends verbatim to any locally Noetherian algebraic stack carrying this data, via any smooth atlas; and (T6) for (g,n) = (6,6) the balanced tetragonal Casnati-Ekedahl datum satisfies the hypotheses: with gamma : C -> P^1_B finite flat of degree 4, relations bundle F fibrewise O(4) direct-sum O(5), the canonical sub-line-bundle L_5 := O_{P^1}(5) tensor q^*q_*(F(-5)) subset F and its quotient L_4 induce a canonical filtration 0 -> W_4 -> W -> W_5 -> 0 of W := (O_{P(E^vee)}(2) tensor gamma^*F^vee)|_C with d_4 = 20 and d_5 = 16 (SRC-0004 Lemma 10.6 convention W_f = (O(2) tensor gamma^*O(-f))|_C), so that (D1) reads 14 > 10 and (D2) reads 10 = 2g-2, phi has ranks 26 -> 12, and Z_ev = a_N^{-1}(e(B)) with N = omega_{C/B} tensor W_5^vee(Gamma), equivalently Z_ev is the scheme-theoretic locus where O_C(Gamma) is isomorphic to W_5 tensor omega_{C/B}^{-1} relatively to B.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Proved steps / lemmas (numbered, exact statements)\\n\\n### Claims (status: proved)\\n\\n**1. CLM-0048-1**  \\n> For pi : C -> B smooth proper with geometrically connected genus-g (g>=1) fibres over a locally Noetherian B, and Gamma the sum of n>=1 disjoint sections, the universal evaluation Phi : p_*L_univ -> p_*(L_univ|_{Gamma_P}) on P = Pic^0_{C/B} with L_univ = omega_{C_P/P}(Gamma_P) tensor Poin^{-1} satisfies Fit_0(coker Phi) subset I_e.\\n\\nJustification:  \\n> Step 3: base change of Fitting ideals along e plus coker(e^*Phi) = R^1pi_*omega_{C/B} tensor M_0^{-1}, invertible, so Fit_0 = 0 and e^*J = 0. No support/radical argument used.\\n\\n**2. CLM-0048-2**  \\n> In the same setting, I_e subset Fit_0(coker Phi); hence Fit_0(coker Phi) = I_e exactly, as ideal sheaves, over arbitrary possibly nonreduced locally Noetherian bases and in arbitrary characteristic.\\n\\nJustification:  \\n> Step 4: at every point b of B and every nonzero xi in T_{e(b)}Pic^0_{C_b/k(b)} = H^1(C_{k(b)},O), coker(iota_xi^*Phi) = H^1(omega tensor N_xi^{-1}) has length 1 by perfectness of the Serre pairing over k(b), so iota_xi^*J = (eps); hence the image of J spans (I_e/I_e^2) tensor k(b); Nakayama over A = O_{B,b} gives I_e = J + I_e^2, and Nakayama over O_{P,e(b)} gives I_e = J. Points off e(B) are handled by the fibrewise cokernel computation.\\n\\n**3. CLM-0048-3**  \\n> Given 0 -> W_4 -> W -> W_5 -> 0 with fibrewise degrees d_4, d_5 and d_4 - n > 2g-2, one has coker(phi) isomorphic to coker(phi_5) and hence Fit_0(coker phi) = Fit_0(coker phi_5); no splitting W = W_4 direct-sum W_5 is required.\\n\\nJustification:  \\n> Step 5: restriction to Gamma is exact (locally split sequence), pi_*