N^{-1}(I_e).O_B, i.e. Z_ev = a_N^{-1}(e(B)) as closed subschemes of B; (T5) formation of both sides commutes with arbitrary base change, and for every locally Noetherian B-scheme T the map T -> B factors through Z_ev if and only if N|_{C_T} is relatively trivial (isomorphic to pi_T^*M for some invertible M on T), whence the identification descends verbatim to any locally Noetherian algebraic stack carrying this data, via any smooth atlas; and (T6) for (g,n) = (6,6) the balanced tetragonal Casnati-Ekedahl datum satisfies the hypotheses: with gamma : C -> P^1_B finite flat of degree 4, relations bundle F fibrewise O(4) direct-sum O(5), the canonical sub-line-bundle L_5 := O_{P^1}(5) tensor q^*q_*(F(-5)) subset F and its quotient L_4 induce a canonical filtration 0 -> W_4 -> W -> W_5 -> 0 of W := (O_{P(E^vee)}(2) tensor gamma^*F^vee)|_C with d_4 = 20 and d_5 = 16 (SRC-0004 Lemma 10.6 convention W_f = (O(2) tensor gamma^*O(-f))|_C), so that (D1) reads 14 > 10 and (D2) reads 10 = 2g-2, phi has ranks 26 -> 12, and Z_ev = a_N^{-1}(e(B)) with N = omega_{C/B} tensor W_5^vee(Gamma), equivalently Z_ev is the scheme-theoretic locus where O_C(Gamma) is isomorphic to W_5 tensor omega_{C/B}^{-1} relatively to B.\\\"\\n\\n3. CLAIMS REJECTED / DOWNGRADED / FLAGGED AS UNPROVED / GAPS\\n------------------------------------------------------------\\nNo checked_claim has verdict other than \\\"confirmed\\\". finding_candidates is empty.\\n\\nHowever, the review does flag scope exclusions and residual sharpness (not fatal rejections of load-bearing claims):\\n\\nFrom exclusions-non-load-bearing (confirmed as exclusions, i.e. NOT licensed as established by ATT-0048):\\n\\\"Nonemptiness, h^0 stratification, dim/components/stabilizers in M_{6,6}, mono/W5D, unbalanced strata, and all Tate/Hodge claims are explicitly excluded; not load-bearing for the stated lemma. No pure-Tate upgrade or omitted stable-pair claim inside the theorem_statement.\\\"\\n\\nFrom strongest_attack (secondary residua