mooth atlas\\\"\\n- strongest_attack residual: \\\"stack 'verbatim identification' means relative triviality of N via Fitting descent, not a_N^{-1}(e) without a Picard stack\\\"\\n\\nCharacteristic / hypotheses:\\n- Theorem opening: \\\"no reducedness, irreducibility or characteristic hypothesis\\\"\\n- Dual-numbers / residue field Serre duality over k used; no char restriction stated in the confirmation notes.\\n\\n6. DIMENSION / CODIMENSION OF Z; COMPONENTS; PURITY; STABILIZERS\\n----------------------------------------------------------------\\n- exclusions-non-load-bearing: \\\"dim/components/stabilizers in M_{6,6} ... are explicitly excluded; not load-bearing for the stated lemma.\\\"\\n- No statement confirming purity of Z, dimension of Z, codimension of Z as a geometric locus in M_{6,6}, or stabilizers.\\n- Target block records ambient numerical targets (not claims about Z's dim/codim as proved by ATT-0048): chow_codimension 13, dimension 21, g=6, n=6, etc. \\u2014 these are packet target metadata, not confirmed geometric conclusions about Z_ev in the checked claims.\\n- Licensed structural description of Z_ev only: scheme-theoretic equality Z_ev = a_N^{-1}(e(B)), with ranks of phi 26 -> 12 at (6,6).\\n\\nstrongest_attack (for context; attack defeated):\\n\\\"Dual-numbers free-module destruction of I_e subset J: misread the LES for H^1(omega tensor N_xi^{-1}) as living over free rank-1 H^1(omega_{C[eps]})\\u2248k[eps] with surjective connecting map, forcing H^1 free of rank 1 and Fit_0=0, which would kill conormal generation and leave only support agreement. Outcome: defeated. The connecting map and dim count are for the underlying O_C-extension (k-vector spaces); Serre duality over the residue field forces dim_k H^1(C_{k[eps]},L)=1, hence the only k[eps]-module of k-dimension 1 is k[eps]/(eps) with Fit_0=(eps). Combined with J subset I_e and the two Nakayamas, this yields scheme-theoretic ideal equality. Secondary residual sharpness (non-fatal): stack 'verbatim identification' means relative triviality of N via Fitting descent, not a_N^{-1}(e) without a Picard stack; L_5 subbundle 'hence' compresses a standard fibrewise-injective-implies-subbundle lemma.\\\"\\n\\n\\n================================================================================\\nREV-0092\\n================================================================================\\n\\n1. HEADER / METADATA\\n--------------------\\nid:                  REV-0092\\ntarget_artifact:     attempt_id = ATT-0048\\nverdict / decision:  \\\"confirmed\\\"\\nreviewer / engine:   reviewer_engine = \\\"qwen\\\"\\nreview_pass:         2\\nreview_task_id:      TASK-V-ATT-0048-P2\\nindependent:         true\\npacket_id:           C66-001-v4\\nsubproblem_id:       C66-GEO-Z\\ncampaign_id:         C66-001 (campaign_revision 4)\\ncreated_on:          2026-08-07\\nfinding_candidates:  [] (empty)\\n\\n2. CLAIMS CONFIRMED AS ESTABLISHED (verbatim)\\n---------------------------------------------\\nAll checked claims have verdict \\\"confirmed\\\".\\n\\nCLM-0048-1 (confirmed):\\n\\\"Step 3: e^*J = Fit_0(coker(e^*Phi)) = Fit_0(R^1 pi_* omega_{C/B} tensor M_0^{-1}) = Fit_0(invertible) = 0, hence J subset I_e. The computation coker(e^*Phi) = R^1 pi_*(omega) tensor M_0^{-1} follows from the long exact sequence of 0 -> omega -> omega(Gamma) -> omega(Gamma)|_Gamma -> 0 twisted by pi^*M_0^{-1}, using R^1 pi_*(omega(Gamma) tensor pi^*M_0^{-1}) = 0 (fibrewise degree 2g-2+n > 2g-2). The trace isomorphism R^1 pi_* omega = O_B gives coker(e^*Phi) = M_0^{-1}, invertible. Fit_0 of an invertible sheaf is 0. This proves J subset I_e without any support argument, defeating the k[eps][x] counterexample template. Correct.\\\"\\n\\nCLM-0048-2 (confirmed):\\n\\\"Step 4: The reverse inclusion I_e subset J is proved by a first-order length computation at every tangent direction followed by Nakayama. For nonzero xi in T_z P_b = H^1(C_k, O), the line bundle N_xi^{-1} on C_{k[eps]} fits in 0 -> O_{C_k} -> N_xi^{