bschemes. Equality of ideals, not point sets. Correct.\\\"\\n\\nCLM-0048-5 (confirmed):\\n\\\"Step 6: T-point criterion. If N|_{C_T} = pi_T^*M' (relatively trivial), then coker(phi_T) = R^1 pi_{T*}(omega) tensor M'^{-1} = M'^{-1}, invertible, so Fit_0 = 0 and T -> B factors through Z_ev. Conversely, if T -> B factors through Z_ev, then Fit_0(coker phi_T) = 0, so a_{N_T}^{-1}(e(T)) = T, i.e. N|_{C_T} is relatively trivial. All constructions commute with arbitrary base change. The stack statement follows from smooth descent for quasi-coherent ideals: let X be a locally Noetherian algebraic stack with the data, u: U -> X a smooth surjection from a scheme. The ideal Fit_0(coker phi) pulls back to U and U x_X U, where the scheme-level theorem applies; quasi-coherent sheaves satisfy smooth descent, so the closed substack Z_ev is well-defined and represents relative triviality of N. Correct.\\\"\\n\\nCLM-0048-6 (confirmed):\\n\\\"Step 7: For balanced tetragonal F fibrewise O(4) + O(5), q_*(F(-5)) is invertible (h^0 = 1, h^1 = 0 fibrewise) and commutes with base change. The counit q^*q_*(F(-5)) -> F(-5) is fibrewise the inclusion of O(0) into O(-1) + O(0), so L_5 := O(5) tensor q^*q_*(F(-5)) -> F has locally free cokernel L_4 (fibrewise O(4)). This gives 0 -> L_5 -> F -> L_4 -> 0, the relative Harder-Narasimhan filtration. Dualizing and twisting by O_{P(E^vee)}(2)|_C (using exactness of gamma^*, gamma finite flat) gives 0 -> W_4 -> W -> W_5 -> 0 with W_4 the sub (built from L_4^vee) and W_5 the quotient (built from L_5^vee). Correct.\\\"\\n\\nCLM-0048-7 (confirmed):\\n\\\"Step 7: At (g,n) = (6,6), SRC-0004 Lemma 10.6 gives deg(W_f|_C) = 4g+12-4f, so d_4 = 20 (f=4) and d_5 = 16 (f=5). (D1): 20-6 = 14 > 10 = 2g-2. (D2): 16-6 = 10 = 2g-2. By (T1), pi_*W has rank 20+16+2-12 = 26, pi_*(W|_Gamma) has rank 12, so Fit_0(coker phi) = I_12(phi). N = omega tensor W_5^vee(Gamma) has fibrewise degree 10-16+6 = 0. Z_ev = a_N^{-1}(e(B)), i.e. scheme-theoretically the locus where O_C(Gamma