other geometric strata or coefficient systems without an exhaustive argument.]\\n\\n(Total: 37 constraint bullets. Several later bullets restate earlier ones in shortened form.)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. ALL \\\"Established facts\\\" entries (verbatim + evidence), grouped by topic\\n\\n### A. Mixed local systems / weight floors / R^1 of punctured curves\\n\\n- R^1 \\u03c0_* Q for the universal n-punctured curve is mixed of weights 1 and 2 (an extension of a rank n-1 Tate system of weight 2 by the rank 2g weight-1 system), never pure of weight 1. The correct weight floor is that H^p(base;L) has weight \\u2265 p+1. [evidence: source; FND-0020]\\n\\n- R^1\\u03c0_*Q for the universal n-punctured curve is mixed of weights 1 and 2 (an extension of a rank n-1 Tate system of weight 2 by the rank 2g weight-1 system), never pure of weight 1; the correct weight floor for H^p(base;L) is therefore \\u2265p+1. [evidence: source; Packet adjudicated finding FND-0020.]\\n\\n### B. Target dictionary: W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}, Poincar\\u00e9 duality, (6,6) numbers\\n\\n- The RED-0001 target W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{g,n}) is a pure polarizable Q-Hodge structure of weight -16; the entire weight-(2d-16) row is pure of that single weight, so polarizable pure Q-HS of fixed weight form a semisimple abelian category and there is no non-split-extension obstruction in this corner. [evidence: source; FND-0033]\\n\\n- The exact open input is W_{-16} H^{BM}_{16}(M_{g,n}), identified by Poincare duality with W_{2d-16} H^{2d-16}(M_{g,n})(d) for d=3g-3+n; for (g,n)=(6,6) one has d=21 and ordinary degree 26. [evidence: source; Packet finding FND-0001 and the packet exact target W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6})=W_{26}H^{26}(M_{6,6})(21).]\\n\\n- For d=3g-3+n, the open Borel\\u2013Moore input W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{g,n};Q) is identified by Poincar\\u00e9 duality with W_{2d-16}H^{2d-16}(M_{g,n};Q)(d). For (g,n)=(6,6) one has d=21, so W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q)=W_{26}H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q)(21). [evidence: source; Packet adjudicated finding FND-0001 together with the packet exact-target dictionary (poincar\\u00e9_twist 21, ordinary degree 26, open BM degree 16).]\\n\\n- The RED-0001 corner W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{g,n}) is a pure polarizable Q-Hodge structure of weight \\u221216; polarizable pure Q-Hodge structures of fixed weight form a semisimple abelian category, so any subquotient of a direct sum of Tate objects in that row is again a direct sum of the same Tate object. [evidence: source; Packet adjudicated finding FND-0033.]\\n\\n### C. vcd / degree 26 vs vanishing above vcd\\n\\n- For RED-0001 residual pairs, the ordinary degree 2d-16 equals vcd for (6,6) (among others) and never exceeds vcd; vanishing above vcd does not kill the target degree 26=vcd(M_{6,6}). [evidence: source; FND-0035]\\n\\n- For (g,n)=(6,6) the required ordinary degree 2d\\u221216 equals the virtual cohomological dimension, so vanishing theorems for degrees strictly above vcd do not by themselves resolve the exact target on M_{6,6}. [evidence: source; Packet adjudicated finding FND-0035 (ordinary degree equals vcd for (6,6)).]\\n\\n### D. Forgetful Leray tower M_{6,6}\\u2192\\u2026\\u2192M_{6,1}; residue SES; Gr^W_{26} surjections\\n\\n- For the forgetful map M_{6,6}\\u2192M_{6,5}, the q=0 term H^{26}(M_{6,5};Q) vanishes because 26>vcd(M_{6,5})=25; fibre cohomology lives only in q=0,1, so no Leray differential enters or leaves total degree 26. [evidence: source; FND-0036]\\n\\n- After q=0 vanishing, the exact target is controlled by the mixed R^1 local system. Although the weight-two quotient has no Gr^W_{26} H^{25} contribution, the connecting map from Gr^W_{26} H^{24} of that quotient can alter the quotient of Gr^W_{26} H^{25} of the weight-one symplectic part; under the five-stage tower those connecting maps affect kernels only of the Gr^W_{26} surjections. [evidence: source; FND-0037; FND-0093]\\n\\n- For (g,n)=(6,6), the five-stage forgetful Leray-plus-residue argument with r=6-j produces a surjection Gr^W_{26} H^{21}(M_{6,1};H^{\\u22975}) \\u21a0 Gr^W_{26} H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q) (weight floor 27 kills residue quotients on Gr^W_{26}). This reduces exact-target vanishing to odd-tensor top-degree vanishing and does not by itself prove the corner. [evidence: source; FND-0093]\\n\\n- Let H be the rank-12 weight-one symplectic local system R^1 of the universal closed genus-6 curve, write V_r=H^{\\u2297r} with V_0=Q, and let f_j:M_{6,j}\\u2192M_{6,j-1} forget the j-th mark. The fibre is a genus-6 curve with j-1 punctures and has cohomology only in degrees 0 and 1. The residue exact sequence of mixed Hodge modules 0\\u2192H\\u2192R_j\\u2192Q(-1)^{j-2}\\u21920 holds for R_j=R^1(f_j)_*Q, and tensoring with V_r yields 0\\u2192V_{r+1}\\u2192V_r\\u2297R_j\\u2192V_r(-1)^{j-2}\\u21920. [evidence: source; Observable argument equations (4)\\u2013(5); diagnostics confirm the residue SES as a short exact sequence of VMHS.]\\n\\n- Fix r=6-j for 2\\u2264j\\u22646. Then d_j+r=26 and d_{j-1}+r+1=26. For coefficients V_r the Leray spectral sequence of f_j has only rows q=0,1; the q=0 term H^{d_j}(M_{6,j-1};V_r) vanishes by the vcd of the base; R^2(f_j)_*Q=0 so no differential enters E_2^{d_{j-1},1}, and outgoing differentials land above d_{j-1}. Hence there is an isomorphism of mixed Hodge structures H^{d_j}(M_{6,j};V_r)\\u2245H^{d_{j-1}}(M_{6,j-1};V_r\\u2297R_j). [evidence: source; Observable argument equations (6) and the vcd vanishing mechanism of packet FND-0036 applied fibrewise in the forgetful tower.]\\n\\n- Morphisms of mixed Hodge structures are strict for the weight filtration. Applying Gr^W_{26} to the long exact sequence of 0\\u2192V_{r+1}\\u2192V_r\\u2297R_j\\u2192V_r(-1)^{j-2}\\u21920 and using vanishing of the residue quotient on Gr^W_{26} yields a surjection Gr^W_{26} H^{d_{j-1}}(M_{6,j-1};V_{r+1})\\u21a0Gr^W_{26} H^{d_{j-1}}(M_{6,j-1};V_r\\u2297R_j). Combined with the Leray isomorphism this gives, for each j=2,\\u2026,6, that Gr^W_{26} H^{d_j}(M_{6,j};V_{6-j}) is a quotient of Gr^W_{26} H^{d_{j-1}}(M_{6,j-1};V_{7-j}). [evidence: source; Observable argument equations (7)\\u2013(8); diagnostics confirm that connecting maps from Gr^W_{26} of the weight-two quotient in degree d_{j-1}-1 alter kernels rather than cokernels once the same-degree graded piece of the residue quotient vanishes.]\\n\\n- On a smooth Deligne\\u2013Mumford stack with constant Q coefficients, H^{26} has weights at least 26, so W_{26}H^{26}=Gr^W_{26}H^{26} in that degree. Therefore vanishing of the source of the composite surjection would imply W_{26}H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q)=0, and by Poincar\\u00e9 duality the exact Borel\\u2013Moore group would be zero (the empty direct sum of Q(8)). [evidence: source; Observable argument equations (10)\\u2013(11) and the final duality conversion; the implication is conditional on source vanishing.]\\n\\n### E. Top weight vs lowest weight (graph complex / CGP)\\n\\n- CGP/tropical/commutative-graph-complex controls top weight gr^W_{2d} H^*, whereas the target is lowest weight gr^W_{2d-16}; for (6,6) these are weight 42 versus weight 26 and never coincide. [evidence: source; FND-0032]\\n\\n### F. Steinberg / filling systems\\n\\n- The standard ordered 0-filling system of 2g arcs a1,b1,...,ag,bg represents the zero class in the Steinberg module St; Broaddus cyclicity uses a different nontrivial generator \\u03c60. Treating the standard filling-system class as a cyclic generator of St does not compute (St \\u2297 V)_G. [evidence: source; FND-0092]\\n\\n### G. Residual CE geometry obligation\\n\\n- Any complete attack on the exact lowest-weight target for (g,n)=(6,6) must still confront residual CE geometry (balanced tetragonal splitting, W_5 failure locus Z, h^0 stratification, components/stabilizers) unless an independent vanishing of the exact corner is proved. [evidence: source; FND-0050]\\n\\n### H. Casnati\\u2013Ekedahl / tetragonal / f=4 vs f=5 / Abel\\u2013Jacobi fibrewise\\n\\n- On any smooth genus-6 degree-four cover C\\u2192P^1 with balanced