2M_{6,1}; residue SES; Gr^W_{26} surjections\\n\\n- For the forgetful map M_{6,6}\\u2192M_{6,5}, the q=0 term H^{26}(M_{6,5};Q) vanishes because 26>vcd(M_{6,5})=25; fibre cohomology lives only in q=0,1, so no Leray differential enters or leaves total degree 26. [evidence: source; FND-0036]\\n\\n- After q=0 vanishing, the exact target is controlled by the mixed R^1 local system. Although the weight-two quotient has no Gr^W_{26} H^{25} contribution, the connecting map from Gr^W_{26} H^{24} of that quotient can alter the quotient of Gr^W_{26} H^{25} of the weight-one symplectic part; under the five-stage tower those connecting maps affect kernels only of the Gr^W_{26} surjections. [evidence: source; FND-0037; FND-0093]\\n\\n- For (g,n)=(6,6), the five-stage forgetful Leray-plus-residue argument with r=6-j produces a surjection Gr^W_{26} H^{21}(M_{6,1};H^{\\u22975}) \\u21a0 Gr^W_{26} H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q) (weight floor 27 kills residue quotients on Gr^W_{26}). This reduces exact-target vanishing to odd-tensor top-degree vanishing and does not by itself prove the corner. [evidence: source; FND-0093]\\n\\n- Let H be the rank-12 weight-one symplectic local system R^1 of the universal closed genus-6 curve, write V_r=H^{\\u2297r} with V_0=Q, and let f_j:M_{6,j}\\u2192M_{6,j-1} forget the j-th mark. The fibre is a genus-6 curve with j-1 punctures and has cohomology only in degrees 0 and 1. The residue exact sequence of mixed Hodge modules 0\\u2192H\\u2192R_j\\u2192Q(-1)^{j-2}\\u21920 holds for R_j=R^1(f_j)_*Q, and tensoring with V_r yields 0\\u2192V_{r+1}\\u2192V_r\\u2297R_j\\u2192V_r(-1)^{j-2}\\u21920. [evidence: source; Observable argument equations (4)\\u2013(5); diagnostics confirm the residue SES as a short exact sequence of VMHS.]\\n\\n- Fix r=6-j for 2\\u2264j\\u22646. Then d_j+r=26 and d_{j-1}+r+1=26. For coefficients V_r the Leray spectral sequence of f_j has only rows q=0,1; the q=0 term H^{d_j}(M_{6,j-1};V_r) vanishes by the vcd of the base; R^2(f_j)_*Q=0 so no differe